## Phase 7: Evaluation & Go/No-Go Decision

**Duration:** 3 weeks (Weeks 36–38)  
**Dependency:** Phase 6 complete; all metrics collected

### Objectives
- Analyze pilot results against success criteria
- Identify key learnings and required changes for scale-up
- Make go/no-go decision on nationwide expansion
- Document roadmap for next phase

### Workstream 1: Impact Analysis

| Question | Data Source | Owner | Duration |
|---|---|---|---|
| Did post-harvest loss decrease? | Farmer survey (2x during pilot) + transaction data | M&E lead | 1 week |
| Did farm-gate price increase? | Transaction prices + farmer survey | Data analyst | 1 week |
| Did payment delays decrease? | Transaction overdue count + farmer/buyer survey | Data analyst | 1 week |
| Did farmers earn more? | Survey: income this season vs. last season, by pilot participant | M&E lead | 1 week |
| Did platform adoption exceed 60% repeat rate? | User login frequency, transaction count per user | Data analyst | 0.5 weeks |
| Did forecasting accuracy reach 60%+? | Recommendation outcome review (did farmers who followed recommendations do better?) | ML engineer | 1 week |

**Deliverable:** Impact summary document with quantified results vs. success criteria

### Workstream 2: Qualitative Feedback & Lessons Learned

| Method | Participants | Owner | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| Farmer Focus Group | 8–10 pilot farmers (mix of engagement levels) | Field ops | "What worked? What was confusing? Would you recommend to a friend?" |
| Buyer/Seller Interviews | 3–5 institutional buyers, 5–8 market sellers | Product | Impact on their business; pricing patterns; transport savings |
| Transporter Feedback | 2–3 transport providers | Field ops | Booking frequency; profitability; usability issues |
| Support Team Debrief | Field ops team + support staff | Field ops lead | Top issues encountered; most frequent user questions; culturally specific blockers |
| Partner Reflection | Farmer group, market association, transport provider leaders | Product + Field ops | Lessons for onboarding; technical requirements; business model adjustments |

**Deliverable:** Qualitative findings document; prioritized list of improvements for scale-up

### Workstream 3: Technical Readiness Review

| Area | Readiness Check | Owner | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| Data Model Scalability | Can Postgres handle 10,000 users, 100,000 transactions? | Backend lead | If yes, migration plan ready for Phase 4; if no, redesign needed |
| USSD Gateway Stability | Did chosen provider meet performance/reliability targets? | Integration eng. | Consider failover or multi-provider strategy if issues |
| Mobile Money Integration | Is payment flow reliable and settlement on schedule? | Finance + Integration eng. | Any fees or chargeback issues to address before scale? |
| Forecasting Model Generalizability | Does model trained on Central Region tomato work for other crops/regions? | ML engineer | Retraining data requirements; model performance on new data |
| Mobile App Performance | App performance acceptable at scale (100+ concurrent users)? | Mobile lead | Any architectural changes needed for 10,000 users? |

**Deliverable:** Technical readiness checklist; list of Phase 4 hardening tasks if scaling

### Workstream 4: Business Model Validation

| Question | Method | Owner | Duration |
|---|---|---|---|
| Are farmers willing to pay a commission or subscription? | Survey with 20+ pilot farmers | Product | Optional at pilot; critical for sustainability at scale |
| Is mobile money provider fee sustainable? | Financial model based on actual transaction volume | Finance | E.g., if 2% provider fee and 5% platform take, is margin positive? |
| Are market associations interested in continuing partnership? | Stakeholder call | Product | What's needed to move from pilot to revenue-sharing partnership? |
| What's the cost per pilot user (marketing, support, data)? | Cost accounting | Finance | How does pilot cost-per-user compare to expected scale cost? |

**Deliverable:** Business model summary; sustainability assessment

### Workstream 5: Go/No-Go Decision Framework

| Scenario | Criteria | Recommendation |
|---|---|---|
| **GO — Scale Up** | Post-harvest loss ↓ by ≥ 15%; farm-gate price ↑ by ≥ 10%; payment delays ↓ to < 10%; repeat usage ≥ 60%; ≥ 80% farmers would recommend; technical readiness OK | Proceed to Phase 3 with additional crops/regions; budget for nationwide expansion |
| **GO — Iterate** | Metrics close (within 5%) but UX issues significant; forecasting accuracy < 60%; specific regions underperform; business model requires adjustment | Proceed to Phase 3 with fixes to identified areas; longer pilot for second region before expansion |
| **NO-GO — Pivot** | Post-harvest loss unchanged or worse; farm-gate price flat/down; adoption < 40% repeat rate; forecast unreliable; key partner(s) withdraw support | Pause expansion; address root causes (e.g., market conditions, political environment, platform fit); consider pivot to different crop or region |

### Phase 7 Deliverables

1. **Evaluation Report** (10–15 pages)
   - Executive summary of results
   - Quantified impact vs. success criteria
   - Qualitative feedback highlights
   - Technical readiness assessment
   - Business model validation
   - Lessons learned (top 5 wins, top 5 challenges)

2. **Roadmap for Next Phase**
   - Recommended scope (crops: tomato only vs. tomato + maize + pepper; regions: Central only vs. Central + Ashanti)
   - Required technical changes before scale (database migration, multi-region deployment, etc.)
   - Organizational changes (hiring, partner additions)
   - Timeline for Phase 3 (adjusted based on findings)

3. **Go/No-Go Recommendation** (1-page decision memo)
   - Clear recommendation (GO, GO-with-conditions, NO-GO)
   - Top 3 decision drivers
   - Stakeholder approval (product lead, sponsor, field ops lead)

### Phase 7 Exit Criteria
- ✅ All pilot data cleaned and analyzed
- ✅ Impact metrics quantified against success criteria
- ✅ Qualitative feedback consolidated and prioritized
- ✅ Technical and business readiness assessments complete
- ✅ Evaluation report approved by stakeholders
- ✅ Go/no-go decision memo signed off and communicated
- ✅ Roadmap for next phase (or pivot) documented
- ✅ Pilot data archived for future reference

